<<~ ahu #/cold-start>>

!! Cold start

# `export LAR_BAGS=/tmp/lar-scratch-<you>` before any `lares` command or in-tree boot — a bare in-tree boot writes projection artifacts into the tracked tree.
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, then `pnpm -r build`, then `pnpm --filter @lararium/tw5 build:tw5-vendor` (the TW5 core blob `head-parity` and `scripts/smoke-plugin-boot.ts` need — `pnpm -r build` does not produce it), then `node tools/stamp-build.mjs`.
# A fresh `git worktree` holds empty submodules (`TiddlyWiki5`, `VSCode-TW5-Syntax`, `mempalace`); populate them before building there.
# `lares-cli` `tests/pour-repave.test.ts` needs the dev-root marker (`LAR_DEV_REPO_ROOT=1` or the gitignored `lar-dev-root.json`).
# The tw5 plugin bundle (`packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/lares-memetic-wikitext.json`, `plugins/standalone/*`, `src/plugin-tiddler.generated.ts`) is tracked and must equal a fresh build — rebuild after any tw5 source or tiddler change and commit it with the change. CI's `build-freshness` job checks it once CI runs.
# Run `bash tools/witness-all.sh` for the whole fleet — a hand-picked subset of witnesses reads greener than the tree.
# Read `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot` (the boot seed), then this carrier, then the rulings memory (`project_grammar_as_tiddlers_rulings.md`) before touching grammar, frame, or ingest code.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/wounds>>

!! Open wounds, by priority

''P1 — owed now, no ruling needed''
* ''Push, then read CI.'' The first CI run on this branch witnesses build-from-clean, the e2e set and bundle freshness for the first time; treat whatever it reds as P1.
* ''`tools/symbol-anchor-witness.sh`'' reads 43 absent symbols against its ceiling of 42; no carrier in the list carries a new anchor and no listed symbol left the source, so the extra count's cause is untraced. Trace it (bisect the witness), then re-aim or retire the carrier it names.
* ''`bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/testing-architecture-scout.mem`'' counts "six" duplicate-named test files; the tree holds ten. Re-true the count and list.
* ''The quoteblock floor in live use.'' `packages/lararium-tw5/src/modules/meme-backstop.ts` `runChildGate` fences a child body whose splice breaks the composed root and raises `quoteblocked` on `surfaceChildGateAlert`; attribution fences only the child whose fence heals the composition. Unit-tested; not yet exercised against real concurrent browser saves — watch it, and add a test for any shape it mis-attributes.
* ''Whole-chunk grain of the floor'' (a carrier arriving whole and partially un-decomposable → fence the whole chunk at the ingest seat) — specified in `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/ahu#/quoteblock-floor`, unbuilt.
* ''The `retired-spelling` fault kind'' and `retiredEnds` name the faults by a history word; consider an invariant name (a spelling outside the frame grammar) across the six files that read it.

''P2 — needs the operator''
* ''The members-board fold'' (`tools/contract-witness.sh`, "A's members board folds B IN"): a vessel's admit-write resolves its board through `nodeNexusIsland` (the charter-keyed island once its charter seats), while `runNexusMembersList` reads its own-key carriage by ruling (a partner's board must never widen this vessel's carriage). A founder whose charter has seated therefore cannot read its own admits. Two rulings meet here; `git log --follow -- packages/lararium-mesh/src/members-board-root.ts` holds the attempts. A ruling on the authority boundary, not a code fix.
* ''Backstop seam (b), PHASE 5'' (`tests/meme-backstop.test.ts`): two child-edit cases the test marks as the operator's call.
* ''Ruling-gated mesh modules'' (listed in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/index.ts`'s header): `contract-relation-witness` (sole user of signing domain `CARRIAGE_RELATION_WITNESS_DOMAIN` — retiring it retires a domain), `recipe`, `readiness`, `reaction-graph` (canon memes pin their mesh `source-file`), `pronaos`, `offering-inspection` (own mesh-namespace memes). Each moves or stays only by ruling.
* ''The capture cell'' sits isolated for review in `packages/lararium-mesh/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-node/src/capture/`, `packages/lararium-tw5/src/capture/`, `packages/lares-cli/src/commands/capture/`. Canon (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/capture-annotation-model`, the sensorium-machina S5 ruling) places capture in Python per stream with the TS @daemon coordinating only; the TS cell is the live path. Rule: retire it to Python, or re-home it.
* ''The wild-bytes line'' — tolerate bytes the house cannot re-make (history, outside bytes), cut tolerance for state it can re-found — awaits canonizing beside the no-legacy law. `packages/lararium-mesh/src/capture/turn-harvest.ts` keeps its retired-head tolerance for old transcripts under it.
* ''`bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/handoff.mem` `#/shift-2026-09-13-meme-hearth`'' (~:516) carries a suspended loop `@_:operator-rebooted-before-steering` (the watcher talk-story) — reconvene or release.

''P3 — deferred by law or by the operator''
* ''The Sensorium's logic'' (`packages/lararium-sensorium/**`, tw5 `form-layer/**`, mesh `ffz-project`, `clock-recovery`, coupling/metric modules): the measure-servo aliases in `ffz-project.ts`, one five-band ladder (Title case `ApertureBand`, the others derived), the `lar_feedback` output field name. Frames inside it stay in scope for healing at any time.
* ''Tangle, the putback law, the tongue fold'' — gated on a real return trip and a whole regeneration of `packages/tree-sitter-memetic-wikitext` (mirror pairing, round-trip CI, Markdown injection into `hana`). The aka/weave rhyme (`memetic-wikitext-framing.mem` Annex) waits on tangle.
* ''A relay-stream profile'' — carriers close on EOT in flight; SYN (`&#x0016;`) stays the one reserved stream mark; the profile defines batch framing and resynchronisation.
* ''A carrier seal'' — re-mint an attestation mark with a computed, verified check when signing lands.
* ''EOT targeting'' — what a resolved `-> to=` would name (the declared-unresolved meaning stands).
* ''A standing whole-tree gate'' (build every package from clean, run every witness and suite) — run as a spirit pass, not built into the CLI or a trigger.

